-- title:
--   The completed natural filtration of a process in $\mathbb R^3$
-- statement:
--   The Brownian filtration of a process $B$ in $\mathbb R^3$: at time $t$, the σ-algebra generated by all coordinates of $B_s$, $s\le t$, completed by the null sets.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The source does not say whether the filtration is completed. The completed one is the usual meaning.
-- source:
--   Bhattacharya, Parisi formula and product-state optimization of quantum mixed p-spin Hamiltonians, manuscript (STOC 2027 submission; held version sha256 ae3fccd2…), §2.1, p.4 (PDF p.4)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ABPOnline_augmentSigma

set_option autoImplicit false

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Set Filter Topology
open scoped NNReal Matrix

namespace QPSpinParisi

/-- The Brownian filtration of a process `B` in `ℝ³` (Bhattacharya, *Parisi formula and product-state optimization of quantum mixed p-spin Hamiltonians*, manuscript (STOC 2027 submission; held version sha256 ae3fccd2…), §2.1, p.4, PDF p.4): the natural filtration of all three
coordinates, completed by the null sets of `P` (`ABPOnline.augmentSigma`).

**Formalization Note** The source says "the Brownian filtration" without saying whether it is completed. The
completed one is the usual meaning. -/
noncomputable def brownVecFiltration {Ω : Type*} [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω)
    (B : Fin 3 → ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) : Filtration ℝ≥0 mΩ where
  seq t := ABPOnline.augmentSigma P
    (⨆ s : ℝ≥0, ⨆ (_ : s ≤ t), ⨆ a : Fin 3, MeasurableSpace.comap (B a s) inferInstance)
  mono' _ _ hst := ABPOnline.augmentSigma_mono P
    (iSup₂_le fun s hs => le_iSup₂_of_le s (hs.trans hst) le_rfl)
  le' _ := ABPOnline.augmentSigma_le P _

end QPSpinParisi


